-## 1. Identity and status
-
-### 1.1 The big picture
-
-BS explores a vast physical-digital world based on his own computer, beginning in unwanted, hostile Jenison. He fights virus regimes, scavenges computer parts, builds machines and architecture, creates vehicles, develops an AI-agent army and restores the Tower's systems. His RTX 4090 Founders Edition becomes a monumental light-restoration landmark. Each claimed region can grow through tables, defenses, transport, production, weapon upgrades and agent activity.
-
-Adam is Brett's remembered brother and safe person, the internal compass and living continuity core of AI-BS. Echos Within supplies personal history, meaning and character inspiration. The computer-world adventure carries that relationship through action, creativity, ordinary enjoyment and continued learning.
-
-Restoring the first Tower is a campaign milestone. New PCs, towers, components and hardware environments provide new worlds. Their stories are generated from established facts and develop through actual events. Earlier enemies can interfere through recorded surviving influence. Building, upgrading and meaningful direction continue after the first restoration.
-
-### 1.2 Status vocabulary
-
-| Label | Meaning |
-| --- | --- |
-| CONFIRMED | The creator explicitly selected or stated this direction; implementation is still unbuilt unless separately verified |
-| PROPOSED | A planning recommendation, example, name, technical design or interpretation awaiting further refinement |
-| VERIFIED ARTIFACT | An inspected document, image or saved file exists; this does not certify its proposed capability |
-| VERIFIED BUILD | A specified capability was compiled and exercised, with scope and evidence recorded |
-| OPEN | An important decision or implementation detail remains unresolved |
-| SUPERSEDED | An earlier proposal conflicts with a later creator direction recorded here |
-| UNVERIFIED | No current runtime/build/hardware evidence establishes the claim |
-
-### 1.3 Present state
-
-Verified artifacts include local planning documents, JSON design registries, thirteen concept images, a supplied Mike appearance reference and a Google Drive collection. Earlier inspection found reusable AI-BS studio, local-chat and browser/Unreal bridge code, but did not establish a complete independent native game runtime. Existing studio/backend functionality is not evidence that this game's systems already work.
-
-The creator authorized starting the custom C++ engine, SDK and creator architecture on 2026-11-01. Microsoft C++ Build Tools and a Windows SDK were installed, and the additive `engine/` subtree compiled in Debug and Release. Verified features are numeric attribute validation, grouped world-edit transactions, revision conflicts, duplicate accepted-command protection, undo/redo, isolated Play copies, scoped in-memory Adam operation metadata, and a bounded fixed-step clock. The SDK installs CMake targets and is used by a separately configured consumer. See [foundation README](../../engine/README.md) and [actual build evidence](../../engine/BUILD_STATUS.md). Revision 0.3 adds stable world/entity UUIDs and local checkpoints preserving world changes, Adam's realized edit history, receipts and undo/redo across restart. Revision 0.4 adds the verified native DX12 window/scene preview. Vehicle simulation, remote companion, graphical creator and campaign simulation remain unimplemented. Earlier toolchain absence is a historical observation superseded by this verified installation/build.
-
-Revision 0.6 adds the verified SDK 0.5 movement subset and current [M0–M11 roadmap](../../engine/BUILD_ROADMAP.md). The full evidence and remaining boundaries are in [PHYSICS_SLICE.md](../../engine/PHYSICS_SLICE.md) and BUILD_STATUS. The first intended release is a private PC alpha: a complete 20–30 minute First Boot chapter through Jenison toward shelter/Pencil Room, starting with telegraphed power faults and repair/isolation or bypass routes. Adam begins with text and sound cues; a native RTX awakening is the initial cinematic showcase. Minimum creator tools enter during that alpha after the route works. None of those later chapter/presentation gates is marked implemented by the movement build.
