+
+Agents use vehicles for supplies, patrol, escort, towing, repair, reinforcement and expedition transport. Route width/height, terrain, coolant access, capacity and current conditions determine suitability. A small skimmer cannot automatically substitute for a heavy tug.
+
+Personal wrecks retain a recoverable core. Some cargo/modules can be permanently lost. Retrieval, towing and rebuilding require appropriate reachable resources and record one vehicle identity so recovery cannot duplicate the original. Rules for agent-owned vehicle cores remain to be specified separately.
