+### 14.1b Persistent native world slice (SDK 0.4.0)
+
+`AIBS::Scene` extracts immutable UUID-bearing box snapshots/meshes and supports nearest ray picking. Composite parts share their persistent parent's UUID. `AIBS::FirstBoot` is a separately linked sample game module, not game rules embedded into the generic engine. It seeds 56 persisted board/core/RAM/GPU/archive/trace/power/slot entities and derives visible illumination from actual core capacity. First Boot repair, relay placement and dismantling all use CreatorSession transactions and preserve realized Adam records. The previous static renderer API remains usable independently.
+
+The native application now loads or initializes `%LOCALAPPDATA%/AI-BS/FirstBootWorld/native-world.aibs` under project `first-boot-world`/branch `main`. It never silently reseeds an existing save. `--checkpoint PATH` chooses a different slot. Its schema/project are separate from the older headless example; existing saves are not reset. Checkpoint format 1 remains unchanged. Optional game validators run before load publication and include both game semantics and render-budget validation.
+
+Native controls: WASD/arrows move, right-drag look, Space/Ctrl elevation, Shift speed, E/left-click interact, B place a relay at the aimed board surface, Delete dismantle a relay, Ctrl+Z/Y undo/redo, F5 save retry, F9 reload, Esc close. A native status/target panel distinguishes SAVED from UNSAVED and shows actual guidance. The bootstrap board is protected from game undo/dismantle; relays can be restored/removed through history. Camera/inspection are transient. There is still no collision, character body, terrain building or full machine assembly.
+
+World edits attempt a synchronous atomic checkpoint and replace the GPU mesh at a fence-safe boundary. Invalid mesh data retains the old mesh. If a save fails, edited state stays visible and UNSAVED; F5 retries, and the last committed checkpoint is preserved. Exiting before a successful retry can lose unsaved changes; close-recovery UI and background persistence are later work. Whole-world history and current file/replay/box budgets remain small-scene constraints.
+
+Verification: eleven native tests per Debug/Release plus installed SDK consumers; nineteen monitor/Qt tests. The eight-process world proof rejects bootstrap undo, repairs/builds, reopens identical pixels/UUIDs/history, undoes/redoes across restart, dismantles and confirms no resurrection. It compares actual GPU pixels before/after repair and before/after rejected mesh replacement, clears/restores an empty scene, and runs with the actual RTX 4090 debug layer. The same sequence passed from the packaged native88 executable. Metadata maps were normalized to the monitor's existing stable_ids-map/entity_ids-list contract; the actual reader confirms the report passes.
+
+Studio v5.329.88 was freshly frozen and smoke-tested with the updated monitor, current executable and shaders, and five existing shortcuts were advanced with originals retained. Older releases remain intact. There was no new website publication in this slice; the web hub remains a dated separate snapshot, not live PC telemetry. The current guide is [engine/README.md](../../engine/README.md); the full ordered path is [BUILD_ROADMAP.md](../../engine/BUILD_ROADMAP.md).
+
+Graphics requirements now include the creator-supplied advanced rendering and standard PC display/control catalogs. They are target capabilities, not implemented toggles or fixed performance promises. Current renderer support remains basic raster/depth/diffuse/emissive-looking colors. Capability-gated graphics preferences must be separate from story/world saves. [Graphics settings roadmap](graphics_fidelity_roadmap.md) records prerequisites, platform checks and future acceptance.
