+### 16.2 First-hour paths
+
+Writing-first discovers a selected memory/catalog route; engineering-first builds independent supply; people-first learns routes or assists NPCs. Each can lead toward a foothold and departures to Archives, Core Sinks or network routes. Escape/confrontation/independence coexist rather than one fixed objective.
+
+Reconcile the graph with the later selected prebuilt skimmer, first salvage/tool, virus encounter, secured node and upgrade table. Time windows remain pacing estimates. Alternate paths can converge without deleting their distinct histories, debt, help, builds and discoveries.
+
+### 16.3 NPCs and side quests
+
+Proposed supportive fictional roles: Caretaker (light/supply), Archivist (catalog/presentation), Courier (routes/deliveries), Tinkerer (machines) and Listener (places to pause). Source-based enemies have their own information, offers and responses. These supportive roles are not automatically family portrayals.
+
+Every interactable NPC has state-aware hints, side-quest opportunity or acknowledgment appropriate to current conditions. Completed repairs should not be requested again; a declined offer should not secretly become debt. Hints can be discovered elsewhere so an encounter with one hostile figure does not become the only route forward.
+
+### 16.4 Outcomes and edit preview
+
+Rules preview affected power, access, navigation, quests, hints, NPC anchors, source-memory provenance, undo and save compatibility. Closing a door, demolishing a machine or building a bridge changes actual dependencies. Quest stages and rule versions require migration/compatibility handling, not silent reinterpretation.
